      "message": "It may be worth mentioning in the commit message that the Library Compliance label configuration in `project.config` on the `refs/meta/config` branch should be updated accordingly.\n\nAlternatively, we could upload a follow-up change directly to `refs/meta/config` and include it under the same topic.\n\nAt the moment, the submit requirement still references a file that is removed by this change:\n\n```\n[submit-requirement \"Library-Compliance\"]\n\tdescription \u003d Changes to specific library/metadata files require additional approval\n\tapplicableIf \u003d -branch:refs/meta/config AND (file:\\\"^lib/.*\\\" OR file:\\\"^WORKSPACE$\\\" OR file:\\\"^.gitmodule$\\\" OR file:\\\"^tools/deps.bzl$\\\")\n```\n\nIn addition, it would be good to verify whether this change has any impact on Gerrit-CI behavior, in particular on how checks are triggered.",
