      "writtenOn": "2026-01-08T17:00:00Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "After this change, the only remaining usage of maven_jar is in the documentation:\n\n```bash\n$ git grep maven_jar.bzl\nDocumentation/dev-build-plugins.txt:load(\"//tools/bzl:maven_jar.bzl\", \"maven_jar\")\n```\n\nMaybe it’s worth mentioning why this isn’t removed as part of this change (including `tools/download_file.py`)?\n\n```bash\n$ git grep download_file.py\ntools/bzl/maven_jar.bzl:        \"_download_script\": attr.label(default \u003d Label(\"//tools:download_file.py\")),\ntools/gjf.sh:    \"$(get_tools_dir)/download_file.py\" -o \"$(get_jar_location $version)\" -u \"$url\" -v \"$sha1\"\n```\n\nI mentioned in another change that we might want to keep both dependency mechanisms for a while—continuing to support the existing `maven_jar` flow for plugin developers alongside the new RJE-based approach. Do we still want to do that, or is the plan to fully switch over in this change?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "719f64275581b78c310bc902affa0014c53a2b69",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
