      "writtenOn": "2026-01-09T21:12:03Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I just want to make sure we’re not removing this accidentally while it’s still needed.\n\nAs long as building plugins inside the Gerrit tree relies on `external_plugin_deps()`, we still depend on the old `maven_jar.bzl` machinery, even though it’s no longer used by Gerrit core itself.\n\nOnce that flow is no longer supported, then we absolutely can (and should) remove `maven_jar.bzl` and its related helpers (`download_file.py`).\n\nSo I’m fully on board with removing it - but only once the plugin-in-tree path has been fully migrated to the new RJE-based approach.",
